  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 Kingsley-Pierson Community School Special Election (September 8, 2026) - Elections - Woodbury County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n \n\n \n\n \n Woodbury County\n Iowa • Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \nDrainage\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Woodbury County\nElections\n\n\n\n Due to staffing and security needs, the ballot drop box is no longer in use. Voted ballots can be returned by mail or in person to 620 Douglas St, Rm 103. Other Election News & Satellite Locations \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections 2026 Kingsley-Pierson Community School Special Election\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \n2017 \n2016 \n2015 \n2014 \n2013 \n2012 \n2011 \n2010 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \nCentral Committee Bylaws\n\n \n \n\n \n2026 Kingsley-Pierson Community School Special Election\n\n \nSeptember 8, 2026\n Special Election \n \n\n A Special Election is any election that is not regularly scheduled. A special election may be held for any purpose authorized or required by law; often to fill a vacancy or for a public measure. \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \nArchived Election Details\n The Kingsley-Pierson Community School District will have a special election to vote on the Physical Plant and Equipment Levy (PPEL) This is a local public measure where district voters decide whether to authorize a dedicated capital funding stream via a tax levy upon all the taxable property within the school district. \nThis is the Public Measure that will appear on the ballot for voters in the Kingsley-Pierson Community School District. \n \n\nPUBLIC MEASURE RB  \n \n\nSHALL THE FOLLOWING PUBLIC MEASURE BE ADOPTED?  \n \n\nShall the Board of Directors of the Kingsley-Pierson Community School District, in the Counties of Plymouth, Woodbury and Cherokee, State of Iowa, for the purpose of purchasing and improving grounds; constructing schoolhouses or buildings and opening roads to schoolhouses or buildings; purchasing of buildings; purchase, lease or lease­purchase of technology and equipment; paying debts contracted for the erection or construction of schoolhouses or buildings, not including interest on bonds; procuring or acquisition of libraries; repairing, remodeling, reconstructing, improving, or expanding the schoolhouses or buildings and additions to existing schoolhouses; expenditures for energy conservation; renting facilities under Iowa Code Chapter 28E; purchasing transportation equipment for transporting students; lease purchase option agreements for school buildings or equipment; purchasing equipment authorized by law; or for any purpose or purposes now or hereafter authorized by law, be authorized for a period of ten (10) years to levy and impose a voter-approved physical plant and equipment tax of not exceeding One Dollar Thirty-Four Cents ($1.34) per One Thousand Dollars ($1,000) of assessed valuation of the taxable property within the school district, and be authorized annually, in combination, as determined by the board, to levy a physical plant and equipment property tax upon all the taxable property within the school district commencing with the levy of property taxes for collection in the fiscal year ending June 30, 2028, and to impose a physical plant and equipment income surtax upon the state individual income tax of each individual income taxpayer resident in the school district on December 31 for each calendar year commencing with calendar year 2027, or each year thereafter? \n \n\nThree Ways to Vote \n \n\nVoters have three options to cast their ballot for this special election: \n \n\n1. Vote by Mail (Absentee Ballot) \n \n \n \nRequest Window: Eligible voters may request a mail-in absentee ballot from now through Monday, August 24 2026, at 5:00 PM. \n \nMailing Date: Ballots requested early will begin mailing on Wednesday, August 19, 2026. \n \nHow to Request: \n \n \nBy Phone: Call the Woodbury County Auditor’s Office at 712-279-6465 to request a form by mail. Note: The request must be made verbally by the eligible voter themselves. \n \nOnline/Print: Download and print the official application form from the Secretary of State Office website. \n \n \n \nSubmission: Return completed and signed request forms by mail or in person to: \n \n \n\nWoodbury County Auditor\n \n620 Douglas St, Rm 103\n \nSioux City, IA 51101 \n \n\n2. Early In-Person Voting \n \n \n \nDates & Times: Wednesday, August 19 through Friday September 4, 2026 (Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM). \n \nNote: The Woodbury County Auditor's Office will be closed on Labor Day, Septemer 7, 2026. \n \nLocation: Woodbury County Courthouse, Auditor’s Office (620 Douglas St, Rm 103, Sioux City). \n \n \n\n3. Election Day Voting \n \n \n \nDate & Times: Tuesday, September 8, 2026, from 7:00 AM to 8:00 PM. \n \nLocation: Eligible voters residing in Precinct 34 (Moville), Precinct 35 (Pierson), and Preconct 36 (Correctionville) must vote at Pierson City Hall, 201 Main Street, Pierson. Only residents of the Kingsley-Pierson Community School District are eligible to vote in this election.  \n \n \n\nFor More Information \n \n\nFor additional details regarding candidate filing or voting procedures, please contact the Woodbury County Elections Division at 712-279-6465. \n \n \n\n \n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n Search Ballots by Precinct Number or Township\n \n\n Moville - Pierson - Correctionville\n \n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Woodbury County, Iowa, Elections website at https://elections.woodburycountyiowa.gov.\n\n\n\n \n\n Woodbury County Courthouse\n\n 620 Douglas St. - Room 103\n \nSioux City, IA 51101\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Woodbury County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8AM - 4:30PM \n \nContact Information\n\n Phone: (712) 279-6465\n \nFax: (712) 2796629 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
